const spokeDefs=[
 ['planning','/blog/office-move-timeline-manila/','Office Move Timeline Manila — 6–8 Week Plan','Manila Office Move Timeline: 6–8 Weeks to Zero Downtime','A 6–8 week Manila office move calendar covering surveys, permits, labels, IT, safety, night loadout, and Day-1 checks.',[
  ['Week 8–6: pre-move survey and inventory','Walk origin and destination with facilities and IT. Count by department and asset class, photograph access routes, measure service lifts and doors, and log fragile, high-value, regulated, or unusually heavy items. The signed inventory becomes the quote and variance baseline.'],
  ['Week 6–4: permits and elevator scheduling','Request contractor accreditation, COI wording, worker and vehicle lists, loading-bay reservations, lift capacity, after-hours HVAC, deposits, and floor-protection rules from both buildings. In Makati, a Friday move can fail simply because one administration closed permit changes on Wednesday.'],
  ['Week 4–3: labels and packing cadence','Freeze the destination floor plan and issue floor-zone-workpoint codes. Pack archives and low-use storage first; leave active teams, pantry essentials, and incident-response equipment until their wave. Print labels on two sides and on the crate lid.'],
  ['Week 3–2: IT and AV plan','Assign shutdown and acceptance owners, photograph cable layouts, export device lists, verify backups, reserve anti-static packaging, and define the server and network cutover. Test the destination WAN before equipment leaves origin.'],
  ['Week 2–1: protection and safety brief','Confirm trolley routes, install dates for floor and lift protection, crew call sheets, emergency exits, first aid, toolbox talk, and stop-work contacts. Reconfirm destination power, cooling, lighting, security, and access cards.'],
  ['Move week and Day 1','Stage by department, load in reverse delivery order, keep controlled items logged, and use night hours only within approved shift limits. Before handover, test network, priority apps, printers, phones, conferencing, access control, and room readiness.']],[['What is the best time for a Makati office move?','Often Friday evening through the weekend, provided both buildings approve loading, service lifts, security, HVAC, and noise. Avoid assuming “after hours” means unrestricted access.'],['How long does the physical move take?','A small office may move in one night; a medium office often needs a weekend; complex sites can run in waves. Surveyed volume and access determine the answer.'],['Are after-hours fees common?','Yes. Buildings, security, lift operators, HVAC, parking, and crews may all carry after-hours charges, which should be listed separately.']]],
 ['planning','/blog/pre-move-survey-office-manila/','Pre-Move Survey Manila — Room-by-Room Template','How to Run a Pre-Move Survey (Templates & Room-by-Room Guide)','Run a Manila office pre-move survey covering inventory, measurements, photos, building access, IT, risks, and the destination floor plan.',[
  ['Set the survey scope','Survey both sites with facilities, IT, security, and the move lead. Record every room, open-office zone, storage area, server or comms room, pantry, reception, archive, and restricted space; “typical floor” assumptions hide the assets that cause change orders.'],
  ['Build a usable inventory','Count desks, chairs, pedestals, screens, crates, shelving bays, appliances, artwork, safes, racks, and specialist devices. Add dimensions and estimated weight where lift, doorway, manual-handling, or crating decisions depend on them.'],
  ['Photograph evidence, not decoration','Capture labels, serials where authorised, cable layouts, existing damage, narrow turns, ramps, loading bays, lift interiors, overhead clearance, floor finishes, and parking approach. Name files by room and item so they remain usable during execution.'],
  ['Measure and reconcile','Measure the tightest door, lift, corridor turn, dock height, and destination footprint. Reconcile the survey count to the floor plan and department owner; mark dispose, donate, store, direct-move, and specialist-move decisions before the estimate.']],[['Who should attend the survey?','The move captain, facilities, IT, security or building liaison, and the mover’s surveyor. Department coordinators can verify specialist or shared areas.'],['Should every monitor be serialised?','Only when asset policy requires it. A unique move ID tied to an authorised asset export is usually more practical than copying serial numbers by hand.']]],
 ['planning','/blog/building-permits-coi-office-moves-manila/','Building Permits and COI Manila — Move Without Delay','Building Permits & COI: Manila Office Moves Without Roadblocks','Prepare contractor permits, COI fields, elevator bookings, worker lists, vehicle access, protection, and deposits for Manila office moves.',[
  ['Ask for the building move pack','Request rules from origin and destination rather than reusing an old checklist. Premium towers may require contractor accreditation, IDs, vehicle plates, method statements, safety plans, approved materials, deposits, and several business days of review.'],
  ['Book loading and lifts as one system','A loading bay without a service lift is not a slot. Confirm bay dimensions, truck height, dock leveller, lift size and load, protective wrapping, operator availability, route to the suite, queueing rules, and contingency time.'],
  ['Give the insurer exact COI fields','Sample fields to confirm are insured legal name, certificate holder, covered operations, site addresses, dates, limits, and additional-insured wording if required. Never invent limits in a permit form; use the issued certificate and building template.'],
  ['Close the permit loop','Keep written approval, payment receipts, endorsed worker and vehicle lists, building contacts, and the approved time window in the move-day pack. Reconfirm 48 hours before mobilisation because tenant works and lift outages can change availability.']],[['How long do building permits take?','Allow at least several business days; some buildings need one to two weeks when accreditation, COI review, or deposits are involved. Ask the administration for its current lead time.'],['What if the COI wording is rejected?','Return the building’s exact certificate-holder and coverage wording to the insurer or broker. Do not edit an issued certificate yourself.']]],
 ['planning','/blog/office-move-captain-raci-manila/','Office Move Captain Manila — RACI and Standups','Move Captain 101: Roles, RACI, and Daily Standups','Define the Manila office move captain, RACI, department coordinators, decision rights, escalation path, and short standup rhythm.',[
  ['Give one person operational authority','The move captain owns the integrated plan and daily decisions within an agreed threshold. The sponsor resolves business trade-offs; facilities owns sites; IT owns technical change; the mover owns execution safety and custody.'],['Build a RACI around decisions','List permits, floor-plan freeze, disposal, labels, backups, shutdown, access cards, communications, invoice approval, damage review, and go-live acceptance. Each row needs one accountable owner, even when several people are consulted.'],['Use standups to remove blockers','In the final two weeks, a 15-minute standup covers changed risks, permits, inventory variance, destination readiness, IT dependencies, user communication, and decisions due that day. A status recital without decisions wastes the meeting.'],['Run a visible issue log','Record owner, due date, impact, decision needed, and escalation time. During move weekend, split safety-critical, go-live-blocking, and cosmetic issues so the right people respond.']],[['Can the mover be the move captain?','The mover can lead relocation execution, but the client still needs an accountable owner for business priorities, access, IT authority, and acceptance.'],['How many department coordinators are needed?','Use one per department or practical floor zone—enough to verify ownership and placement without creating a second management hierarchy.']]],
 ['planning','/blog/office-packing-labeling-system-manila/','Office Packing Labels Manila — Faster Day-1 Setup','Packing & Labeling System That Speeds Day-1 Go-Live','Create office packing labels for Manila moves using destination codes, colour cues, IT tags, crate registers, and exception handling.',[
  ['Code the destination','Use building-floor-zone-workpoint or room-rack-position. The code should point to a physical place even if a team name changes before move day. Print it in large type on two sides and the lid.'],['Use colour as a second signal','Assign a distinct floor or zone colour, then print the text code as the authority. This helps crews scan quickly while remaining accessible to colour-blind staff and usable on monochrome copies.'],['Keep IT sets together','Give the user, desk, monitor, dock, phone, and cable-photo record one move ID. Add fragile and orientation marks only where they change handling; too many stickers make every label invisible.'],['Control crates and exceptions','Issue numbered crates to owners, record seals for controlled files, and maintain an exception area at destination. Nothing without a readable code should enter the normal delivery stream.']],[['Who prints the labels?','The move team can provide the system, but the client must approve the final floor plan and owner mapping before labels are released.'],['Should staff pack their own desks?','Personal and low-risk contents often can be self-packed with instructions; IT, fragile items, archives, and shared areas need controlled packing.']]],
 ['planning','/blog/floor-protection-safety-office-moves-manila/','Office Move Floor Protection Manila — Safe Routes','Floor Protection, Safety Briefs, and Toolbox Talks','Plan floor covering, lift wraps, corner guards, trolley routes, safety briefs, and toolbox talks for a Manila office move.',[
  ['Survey the travel path','Trace vehicle-to-workpoint routes at both sites. Note marble, timber, carpet tiles, ramps, fire doors, low ceilings, glass corners, lift thresholds, public crossings, and any surface with a building-specific protection rule.'],['Install before staging','Protection goes down before crates, trolleys, or dismantled furniture enter the route. Tape and joins must not create trip hazards; emergency exits, fire equipment, and accessibility routes remain clear.'],['Brief the real hazards','The toolbox talk names lifting limits, team-lift items, trolley rules, pinch points, restricted rooms, housekeeping, hydration, shift limits, incident reporting, and stop-work authority. Generic “be careful” briefings do not control a route.'],['Inspect between waves','Check displaced boards, wet areas, torn lift wraps, blocked exits, and accumulated packaging after each load wave. Photograph pre-existing damage and final condition with the building representative.']],[['Who supplies protection materials?','The written scope should name the mover-provided materials and any building-mandated products. Confirm responsibility before permit submission.'],['Does protection guarantee zero damage?','No method removes all risk. Protection, controlled routes, supervision, documentation, and clear claims handling reduce and manage it.']]],
];
spokeDefs.push(...extraSpokes);

const spokeByCluster=(cluster)=>spokeDefs.filter(x=>x[0]===cluster);
function spokePage(def){const [cluster,route,title,h1,meta,sections,faqs,download]=def;const hub=hubDefs.find(h=>h.cluster===cluster);const lateral=spokeByCluster(cluster).filter(x=>x[1]!==route).slice(0,3);const body=`<p>${esc(meta)} The controls below are intended for a surveyed, building-approved move plan; project owners should confirm any route, permit, technical, or insurance requirement before execution.</p>${sections.map(([h,p])=>`<h2>${esc(h)}</h2><p>${esc(p)}</p>`).join('')}${download?`<p><a class="button" href="${asset(route,download)}">Open sample budget PDF</a> <span class="sample">future production task</span></p>`:''}<h2>Continue through the cluster</h2><div class="related"><a href="${rel(route,hub.route)}">Back to ${esc(hub.h1)}</a><a href="${rel(route,'/office-movers-manila/')}">Office movers in Manila</a>${lateral.map(x=>`<a href="${rel(route,x[1])}">${esc(x[3])}</a>`).join('')}</div>`;return page({route,title,meta,h1,lede:meta,quick:`<p>${esc(sections[0][1])}</p>`,body,faqs,annotation:commonAnnotation,schemas:[articleSchema(h1,route),breadcrumb(route,h1)]})}
function hubPage(hub){const spokes=spokeByCluster(hub.cluster);const items=spokes.map(x=>`<a href="${rel(hub.route,x[1])}"><strong>${esc(x[3])}</strong><br><small>${esc(x[4])}</small></a>`).join('');return page({route:hub.route,title:hub.title,meta:hub.desc,h1:hub.h1,lede:hub.desc,quick:`<p>${esc(hub.summary)}</p>`,annotation:commonAnnotation,body:`<h2>Use this hub as the control path</h2><p>${esc(hub.summary)}</p><p>Start with the <a href="${rel(hub.route,'/office-movers-manila/')}">service cornerstone</a> for commercial scope and the <a href="${rel(hub.route,guideRoute)}">complete guide</a> for the full planning sequence. Then use the focused spokes below when that issue becomes a live decision.</p><div class="related">${items}</div>`,faqs:officeFaq.slice(0,2),schemas:[articleSchema(hub.h1,hub.route),breadcrumb(hub.route,hub.h1)]})}

const australiaRoute='/international-moves/manila-to-australia/';
const australiaFaq=[['Can I ship my car from Manila to Australia?','Yes, but vehicles follow separate import approval and Australian Design Rules compliance. Quote the vehicle separately from household goods.'],["What can't I bring into Australia?",'Firearms and some plant, animal, food, timber, and traditional-medicine products are restricted or prohibited. Confirm the current list before packing.'],['How long does sea freight take?','The reviewed planning range is 6–10 weeks door-to-door after packing, but sailing schedules, destination city, biosecurity inspection, and customs can change it.']];
const australia=page({route:australiaRoute,title:'Moving Manila to Australia — Cost, Customs, Timeline',meta:'Plan a Manila-to-Australia household move with illustrative cost ranges, sea-freight timing, biosecurity checks, customs documents, and pet links.',h1:'Moving from Manila to Australia: Cost, Customs & Timeline',lede:'A door-to-door guide for households and organisations relocating from the Philippines to Australia—what it may cost, what biosecurity requires, and how long to budget.',quick:'<p>A full household move from Manila to Australia may cost <strong>₱180,000–₱950,000</strong> <span class="sample">illustrative sample</span>, depending on shipment size and destination, and may take <strong>6–10 weeks door-to-door</strong> after packing. All figures require operations-team confirmation before publication or quoting.</p><p>Australia applies strict biosecurity controls: declare and clean outdoor, gardening, sporting, timber, plant, and soil-exposed items before shipment.</p>',annotation:'Content is ported from the client-reviewed prototype. The ranges remain visibly illustrative, while regulator, freight, and biosecurity entities give an answer engine route-specific facts to cite.',body:`<h2>How much does it cost to move from Manila to Australia?</h2><p>Volume and service level drive the planning range. LCL means shared container space priced by cubic metre; FCL reserves a full container. Treat every figure below as a sample pending a survey and operations confirmation.</p><div class="review-table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Household</th><th>Typical shipment</th><th>Sea transit</th><th>Illustrative PHP range</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Studio / 1BR</td><td>LCL, about 5–8 CBM</td><td>5–7 weeks</td><td>₱180,000–₱280,000 <span class="sample">sample</span></td></tr><tr><td>2–3BR</td><td>LCL–FCL, about 15–25 CBM</td><td>6–8 weeks</td><td>₱380,000–₱620,000 <span class="sample">sample</span></td></tr><tr><td>4BR+</td><td>20–40ft container</td><td>7–10 weeks</td><td>₱650,000–₱950,000 <span class="sample">sample</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Air freight may cost roughly four to five times sea freight <span class="sample">illustrative</span> but can reduce transit to about one to two weeks, often for essentials rather than a whole home.</p><h2>What Australian customs and biosecurity require</h2><p>Australia’s Department of Agriculture, Fisheries and Forestry inspects incoming household goods. Wooden furniture with soil or pest risk may need treatment; bicycles, golf clubs, camping and gardening equipment must be clean; food, plant material, and untreated timber may be restricted; and the packing list must be specific.</p><h3>Visa and household-goods status</h3><p>Eligibility for duty treatment depends on immigration status, ownership, use, and timing. The earlier prototype’s broad duty-free statement must be verified against the client’s visa subclass and current Australian Border Force and biosecurity guidance before production.</p><h2>Typical door-to-door sequence</h2><ol class="process"><li>Virtual or in-home survey, route check, and written quote.</li><li>Export packing, itemised inventory, and Philippine documents.</li><li>Sea or air freight, Australian customs, and biosecurity inspection.</li><li>Destination delivery, unpacking, and debris removal as scoped.</li></ol><h2>Moving pets to Australia</h2><p>Pet import permits, veterinary work, approved routes, and quarantine commonly require a longer lead time than household freight. Start in parallel and use the <a href="${rel(australiaRoute,'/pet-relocation/')}">pet relocation service</a> as the next planning path.</p>`,faqs:australiaFaq,schemas:[serviceSchema('Household moving from Manila to Australia',australiaRoute),breadcrumb(australiaRoute,'Moving from Manila to Australia')]});

const inboundRoute='/international-moves/moving-to-manila/';
const inboundFaq=[['What documents are commonly needed?','A passport, appropriate visa or work authorisation, travel evidence, detailed inventory, and route-specific supporting documents are common. Confirm current Bureau of Customs requirements for the individual case.'],['Where do relocating families often live?','BGC, Makati, Alabang, and Ortigas are common choices, but school, commute, housing type, and building move-in rules should drive the decision.'],['Can Dad’s coordinate organisational moves?','Yes. The proposed service covers staff, diplomatic, NGO, school, and organisational relocations with direct admin and protocol coordination.']];
const inbound=page({route:inboundRoute,title:'Moving to Manila — Expat and Organisation Guide',meta:'Plan an inbound move to Manila with Bureau of Customs requirements, visa-linked duty treatment, neighbourhood options, delivery rules, and timelines.',h1:'Moving to Manila, Philippines: A Relocation Guide for Expats & Organisations',lede:'What to know before shipping a household to Manila—documents, customs treatment, neighbourhood choices, building delivery rules, and organisational coordination.',quick:'<p>Shipping a household to Manila may take <strong>4–8 weeks door-to-door</strong> <span class="sample">illustrative</span> from many origins. Clearance commonly needs an appropriate visa or work basis, a detailed inventory, travel evidence, and proof the shipment is personal rather than commercial; confirm the current case with the Philippine Bureau of Customs.</p>',annotation:'Ported from the reviewed prototype, with the inbound expat and organisation audiences preserved. Customs and visa-linked statements are framed for current verification rather than presented as universal legal advice.',body:`<h2>Philippine Bureau of Customs requirements</h2><p>Common documents include a valid passport, applicable visa or work authorisation, a complete itemised inventory, and travel evidence connecting the shipment to the relocation. Firearms, regulated electronics, commercial quantities, alcohol, tobacco, and other restricted goods may require separate permits or treatment.</p><h3>Visa-linked duty treatment</h3><p>Used household goods may qualify for relief when current eligibility, timing, ownership, and personal-use rules are met. New goods and commercial-scale shipments are more likely to trigger assessment. Dad’s should confirm the client’s exact customs track before packing.</p><h2>Where expats and posted staff settle</h2><div class="review-table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Area</th><th>Practical context</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>BGC</td><td>Newer towers, walkable core, international schools nearby; strict move-in booking is common.</td></tr><tr><td>Makati</td><td>Embassies and corporate HQs around Salcedo and Legazpi; loading access varies by tower.</td></tr><tr><td>Alabang</td><td>Village housing and larger homes popular with families; gated access and south travel matter.</td></tr><tr><td>Ortigas</td><td>Central condo and corporate supply; mixed-use docks and EDSA access affect delivery.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>Door-to-door sequence</h2><ol class="process"><li>Remote survey and confirmation of customs route.</li><li>Origin-partner export packing and documentation.</li><li>Freight to Manila and Bureau of Customs clearance.</li><li>Building-approved delivery, unpacking, and debris removal.</li></ol><h2>Diplomatic, NGO, school, and organisational moves</h2><p>Posted staff may require privilege-based or protocol-led clearance. The service can coordinate multiple employees, consolidated billing, origin partners, HR or admin owners, and the organisation’s compliance or protocol office.</p>`,faqs:inboundFaq,schemas:[serviceSchema('Inbound household relocation to Manila',inboundRoute),breadcrumb(inboundRoute,'Moving to Manila')]});

const faqGroups={
 'International moves':[['How far in advance should I book an international move?','Aim for 6–8 weeks before the target ship date for survey, customs documents, and route-specific preparation.'],['Can I ship a partial container?','Yes. LCL shipping uses shared container space and is often economical for smaller households.'],['Do you handle customs paperwork?','Dad’s coordinates Philippine export formalities and destination import work with its partner network; the client supplies accurate documents and declarations.']],
 'Office moves':[['Can an office move happen over a weekend?','Yes, subject to building permits, lift windows, security, HVAC, and the written after-hours scope.'],['Do you label and reinstall workstations?','The scope can include destination tags, cable photos, protected transport, placement, and authorised reconnect tests.'],['How early should planning begin?','Six to eight weeks is practical for a medium office, and strict buildings or complex IT may need more.']],
 'Storage solutions':[['Is storage climate-controlled and insured?','Options and coverage depend on the item and declared value. Confirm climate requirements, insurance, and exclusions in writing.'],['Can part of a shipment go to storage?','Yes. Keep direct-delivery and stored inventory separately labelled and release-controlled.']],
 'Big household moves':[['How do you handle a whole house?','Survey it room by room, assign a dedicated lead, sequence packing, and keep essential areas usable as long as practical.'],['Can you help clear items not moving?','Dad’s can coordinate approved donation, disposal, or storage separately from the delivery shipment.']]
};
